{title: 481 - Dear Lord and Father}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[C]Dear Lord and Father of mankind,
[G7/B]Forgive [C]our feverish [G]ways;
[C]Reclothe us in our rightful [F]mind,
[F]In purer lives [D7/C]Thy [G/B]service [C]find,
[C/E]In deeper [F]reverence, [C]praise.

Verse 2:
[C]In simple trust like theirs who [D7]heard,
[G7/B]beside [C]the [Am]Syrian [G]sea,
[C]the gracious calling of [Em]the [F]Lord,
[F]let us, like [Dm]them, [D7/C]without [G7/B]a [C]word,
[C/E]rise [F]up and follow [C]thee.

Verse 3:
[C]O sabbath rest by Galilee,
[G7/B]O [C]calm of [Am]hills above,
[C]where Jesus knelt to share [Em]with [F]thee
[F]the silence [Dm]of [D7/C]eternity,
[C/E]interpreted [G7/F]by [C]love!

Verse 4:
[C]Drop thy still dews of quietness,
[G7/B]till [C]all our [Am]strivings [G]cease;
[C]take from our souls the strain [Em]and [F]stress,
[F]and let our ordered [D7/C]lives [G7/B]confess
[C/E]the [F]beauty of [G7/F]thy [C]peace.

Verse 5:
[C]Breathe through the heats of our desire
[G7/B]thy [C]coolness [Am]and thy [G]balm;
[C]let sense be dumb, let flesh [Em]retire;
[F]speak through the [Dm]earthquake, [G/B]wind, [G7/B]and [C]fire,
[C/E]O [F]still, small voice [G7/F]of [C]calm.
